  "goodToKnow": "Die Grotte is a grotto, a picturesque or artificial cave. King Ludwig II of Bavaria built the Venusgrotte at Linderhof, inspired by Wagner's opera Tannhäuser, with an artificial lake, coloured lighting and a shell-shaped boat. Natural caves are mostly called Höhlen. The slang grottenschlecht means dreadfully bad. Plural: die Grotten."
